{"title":"Find The Minimum Possible Sum Of A Beautiful Array","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given positive integers n and target. An array nums is beautiful if it meets the following conditions: nums.length == n. nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers. There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, in the range [0, n - 1], such that nums[i] + nums[j] == target. Return the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have modulo 10^9 + 7.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 2, target = 3\nOutput: 4\n```\n\nExplanation: We can see that nums = [1,3] is beautiful. - The array nums has length n = 2. - The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers. - There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3. It can be proven that 4 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 3, target = 3\nOutput: 8\n```\n\nExplanation: We can see that nums = [1,3,4] is beautiful. - The array nums has length n = 3. - The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers. - There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3. It can be proven that 8 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: n = 1, target = 1\nOutput: 1\n```\n\nExplanation: We can see, that nums = [1] is beautiful.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= n <= 10^9\n- 1 <= target <= 10^9\n\nA beautiful array has n distinct positive integers and no two distinct entries sum to target. Return the minimum possible sum. The minimum set takes the smallest allowed values below target, then uses values from target upward.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def minimumPossibleSum(self, n: int, target: int) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().minimumPossibleSum","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"},{"name":"target","type":"int"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[1,1],"expected":1},{